---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n';

const strings = t('en');
---

<BaseLayout title={strings.meta.cookieTitle} locale="en">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mb-8">{strings.meta.cookieTitle}</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none space-y-6 text-neutral-700">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> March 11, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This Cookie Policy describes the types of cookies and similar technologies used by the website
        <strong>pawmeet.io</strong> (hereinafter, the "Site") and by the administration panel reserved
        for authorized personnel. This policy is drafted in compliance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679
        ("GDPR"), Italian Legislative Decree 196/2003 as amended by Legislative Decree 101/2018, and the
        Italian Data Protection Authority's cookie guidelines of June 10, 2021.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">1. Data controller</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is <strong>Cervera Studio</strong>,
        VAT IT04904730167.
      </p>
      <p>
        For any cookie-related questions, you can contact us at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@pawmeet.io" class="text-primary underline">privacy@pawmeet.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">2. What are cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files that websites store on the user's device (computer, tablet, or smartphone)
        during browsing. They serve to store useful information to improve the browsing experience or for the
        technical operation of the site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">3. Types of cookies</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>By purpose:</strong> technical cookies (necessary for operation), analytics cookies
          (traffic measurement), profiling cookies (preference tracking).</li>
        <li><strong>By duration:</strong> session cookies (deleted when browser closes) and persistent
          cookies (remain until expiry or manual deletion).</li>
        <li><strong>By origin:</strong> first-party cookies (set by the visited domain) and third-party
          cookies (set by different domains).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">4. Cookies used by the website (pawmeet.io)</h2>
      <p>
        The PawMeet public website is a static informational page (SSG) hosted on Cloudflare Pages.
        <strong>It does not install first-party cookies, analytics cookies, or profiling cookies.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare infrastructure may set strictly necessary technical cookies for the security and
        operation of the CDN network:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b">
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Cookie</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Provider</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Duration</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2">Type</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Cloudflare</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Anti-bot protection (Bot Management). Distinguishes human traffic from automated traffic.</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">30 minutes</td>
              <td class="py-2">Technical, third-party</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">5. External resources</h2>
      <p>
        The typefaces used on this site (Inter and Instrument Serif fonts) are self-hosted on our
        servers via Fontsource. No requests are made to third-party servers for font loading, and
        therefore no user data is transmitted to external parties for this purpose.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">6. Administration panel cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The administration panel (backoffice), accessible only to authorized PawMeet personnel, uses
        technical cookies for authentication management (<code>admin_refresh_token</code> and <code>admin_session</code>).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">7. Mobile app</h2>
      <p>
        The PawMeet mobile app <strong>does not use cookies</strong>. Session data and preferences are
        managed locally through native device technologies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">8. Profiling and analytics cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Currently, the website and administration panel <strong>do not use profiling cookies, third-party
        analytics cookies, or tracking tools</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">9. How to manage cookies</h2>
      <p>
        You can manage cookie preferences directly through your browser settings. Please note that
        disabling technical cookies may compromise the operation of some parts of the site.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Chrome</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Safari</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft Edge</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">10. Legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Technical cookies used on the Site and administration panel are installed on the basis of the
        exemption for strictly necessary cookies and the legitimate interest of the controller to ensure
        the security and operation of its services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">11. Data subject rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Articles 15-22 of the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict,
        port, and object to the processing of your personal data. Contact us at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@pawmeet.io" class="text-primary underline">privacy@pawmeet.io</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">12. Policy updates</h2>
      <p>
        The Controller reserves the right to update this Cookie Policy at any time. In case of substantial
        changes, notice will be given through the Site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">13. Contact</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@pawmeet.io" class="text-primary underline">privacy@pawmeet.io</a></li>
        <li>Web: <a href="https://cervera.studio" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cervera.studio</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-12 border-t pt-6">
        This Cookie Policy complies with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), Italian Legislative Decree 196/2003
        and subsequent amendments, and the Italian Data Protection Authority's cookie guidelines
        (provision no. 231 of June 10, 2021).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
